package concept

heat_and_work: {
  content: #"""
    *Heat* and *work* are two ways energy is transferred across the boundary of
    a system. They describe a process, not energy stored in the system; the
    amounts transferred can depend on the path between the initial and final
    states.

    - *Heat* is energy transferred because of a temperature difference. In this
      handbook, $Q > 0$ when the system absorbs heat and $Q < 0$ when it releases
      heat.
    - *Work* is energy transferred when forces acting through displacements
      change the system or its surroundings. In this handbook, $W > 0$ when the
      system does work on its surroundings and $W < 0$ when the surroundings do
      work on the system. For example, a gas expanding against a piston does
      positive work under this convention.
  """#
  related: [
    "concept/state-function",
    "concept/thermodynamic-process",
    "concept/thermal-system",
    "concept/internal-energy",
  ]
}
